WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:16.000
A focused tool service for a larger agent workflow. CV tailoring is the current illustration of the idea.

2
00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:32.000
The tool is one capability the agent uses. It does not need to own the conversation or every step of the business process.

3
00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:48.000
This is a conceptual service boundary, not a published API schema. The actual input and output contract would be agreed during implementation.

4
00:00:48.000 --> 00:01:04.000
Use a job posting as the target and a saved profile as evidence. Emphasize relevant experience without inventing qualifications.

5
00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:20.000
The existing seven-step visualization covers a job posting, saved CV evidence, tailored CV, cover letter, advisory review, optional saving and PDF export.

6
00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:36.000
Human review is part of the intended workflow. The original advisory ATS score uses fabricated data; it is not an employer result or a hiring prediction.

7
00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:52.000
Other document types need their own sources, templates and review rules. They should be scoped and validated separately.

8
00:01:52.000 --> 00:02:08.000
Start with one document type and one clear use case. We can design the tool around your agent, your source material and your approval process.
